{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf5hDx3oUnVkWbMApSfr9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me review my findings and create a comprehensive analysis summary.\n\n## ANALYSIS Summary\n\n**Requirement:** Add a `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint that moves a shipment from CREATED to CONFIRMED status, handles idempotent retries, and rejects invalid state transitions.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- `Shipment.kt:9-27` - Entity with status field (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- `ShipmentController.kt:20-56` - Existing endpoints follow Spring RestController pattern\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27` - In-memory store with save/findById/existsById methods\n- `ApiExceptions.kt:18-24` - ConflictException (409), ResourceNotFoundException (404)\n- `ApiError.kt:31-37` - ErrorCode enum (closed set, part of public contract)\n- `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:14-28` - Centralized exception-to-response mapping\n- `ShipmentControllerTest.kt:23-84` - Test pattern using MockMvc with status/jsonPath assertions\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n1. Controllers throw ApiException subclasses; GlobalExceptionHandler catches them\n2. ConflictException → HTTP 409, ResourceNotFoundException → HTTP 404\n3. Error codes defined in closed ErrorCode enum; each is part of the API contract\n4. Test pattern: @SpringBootTest, @AutoConfigureMockMvc, repository injection with @BeforeEach reset\n5. Status assertions (isCreated, isConflict, isNotFound, isOk) and jsonPath for response validation\n\n**Affected files (cannot be avoided):**\n1. `ShipmentController.kt` - add POST `/{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint\n2. `ApiError.kt` - add error code for invalid shipment status (e.g., SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS)\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` - add 4+ tests for: CREATED→CONFIRMED, CONFIRMED→CONFIRMED (idempotent), CANCELLED→409, unknown→404\n\n**Risks:**\n1. Adding ErrorCode to closed enum is a public API change (but required by the ticket)\n2. Idempotent behavior on CONFIRMED must be implemented correctly\n3. Must verify CANCELLED shipments can only be set in tests (no cancel endpoint yet)\n\n**Open questions:** None — all cases are clearly defined by the ticket.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** - Add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` to ErrorCode enum (line 31-37). This code will be thrown when confirming a CANCELLED shipment, making the HTTP 409 reason machine-readable for clients.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** - Add a new handler method `confirmShipment` (after line 52):\n   - `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` \n   - Finds shipment by ID; throws ResourceNotFoundException if not found (404)\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throws ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS (409)\n   - If status is CREATED, saves it with status CONFIRMED\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, does nothing (idempotent)\n   - Returns ResponseEntity.ok() with the shipment (unchanged for CONFIRMED, updated for CREATED)\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Add 4 test methods after line 83:\n   - `confirms_a_created_shipment_and_returns_it` - POST confirm on CREATED → 200 with CONFIRMED status\n   - `confirm_is_idempotent_on_confirmed_shipment` - POST confirm on CONFIRMED twice → both 200, no change\n   - `rejects_confirming_a_cancelled_shipment_with_conflict` - POST confirm on CANCELLED → 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS\n   - `rejects_confirming_unknown_shipment_with_not_found` - POST confirm on missing ID → 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n**Alternative rejected:** Could have added a `updateStatus(id, newStatus)` method to the repository and used it from the controller. Rejected because: (1) the ticket specifically names the confirm operation, not a generic status update; (2) adding a generic method would be overengineering for a single transition; (3) keeping it simple in the controller keeps the business logic in one place.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | Response | Mechanism |\n|------|------|-------|----------|-----------|\n| CREATED→CONFIRMED | findById(id) | save(shipment with CONFIRMED) | 200 with shipment | ResponseEntity.ok() |\n| CONFIRMED→CONFIRMED | findById(id) | (none) | 200 with shipment | ResponseEntity.ok() |\n| CANCELLED→? | findById(id) | (none) | 409 Conflict | throw ConflictException |\n| Unknown ID | findById(id)=null | (none) | 404 Not Found | throw ResourceNotFoundException |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- **Test 1** (confirm_created): Create shipment, POST confirm, assert 200 and status=CONFIRMED\n- **Test 2** (confirm_idempotent): Create shipment, POST confirm twice, assert both 200, database shows CONFIRMED once\n- **Test 3** (confirm_cancelled): Manually write CANCELLED shipment to repository, POST confirm, assert 409 and error code\n- **Test 4** (confirm_not_found): POST confirm on unknown ID, assert 404 and error code\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":636,"cache_read_input_tokens":16918,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":636},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"65cc952e-792a-4fbd-962e-ee06e650dbff","uuid":"c1b16b49-1a2a-4b38-ab6d-e2ff5707d090","timestamp":"2026-09-15T18:25:39.014Z","request_id":"req_011Cf5hDwUa8JTNykHhn7sjE"}
